course: dictionary
lesson: 5292
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Junior is one of them. Its meaning changes with the words around it, so the context tells you which meaning to use. «Junior parkrun is a free 2 km run on Sunday mornings for ages 4 to 14.» Here junior means for younger people, because the run is for children and the adult one is on Saturday.
explain: In «Sam is three years my junior», junior means younger than me. A junior doctor is newer in the job and less senior, so junior means lower in rank. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some words also come from different places. In the UK, «junior school» is the school for children about 7 to 11. In the US, a junior is a student in the third year of a four-year high school or college. Always check the clues, and use a dictionary when the context does not settle it.
fact: Junior can mean younger, or for younger people: «junior school» is the primary school for children about 7 to 11 in the UK, Ireland and Australia.
fact: Junior can mean lower in rank or less experienced, as in «junior doctor».
fact: In the US and Canada, a junior is a student in the third year of a four-year high school or college.
fact: In the US, «Junior» (Jr.) is added after the name of a son who has the same name as his father.
fact: Juniors in England play 7 against 7 at Under-9 and Under-10, and 9 against 9 at Under-11 and Under-12.
exercise: «Junior parkrun is a free 2 km run on Sunday mornings for ages 4 to 14.» In this sentence, junior means | A son with the same name as his father | *Younger, for younger people | A third-year student | Lower in rank at work
exercise: A new doctor who is still learning is called a junior doctor. What does junior mean here? | Very old | Younger than 7 | *Less experienced, lower in rank | Fast at running
exercise: «Mill Lane Juniors play Station Road Rovers every May.» Who are the juniors in this sentence? | A type of pitch | Teachers at a school | Grown-up referees | *Young players in a team
test: Sam says, «Sam is three years my junior.» What does junior mean here? | The same age as me | Lower in rank at work | Older than me | *Younger than me
test: In the US, a son with the same name as his father may be called «Junior» (Jr.). What does Junior show? | *A son with the same name as his father | A student in the first year of college | A football team for under-11s | A school for small children
exam: Which meaning of junior fits «junior school» in England? | A nursery for babies under 3 | A school only for adults | A secondary school for teenagers | *A primary school for children about 7 to 11
